No line break right after opening punctuation (UAX #14 LB14): brackets and opening quotes, the CJK and fullwidth ones
too (`(`, `[`, `{`, `“`, `«`, `„`, `「`, `【`, `（` ...), keep to the word after them, as upstream already keeps closing
punctuation to the word before it (LB13). Without it a line could end between the two brackets of `[[account]]`. Every
wrapping path takes it: `LineWrapper::wrap_line`, the shaped line's `LineLayout::compute_wrap_boundaries`, which every
wrapped text element draws with, and `LineWrapper::truncate_wrapped_line`, so a clamped label is cut where it wraps. A
run of opening brackets longer than the line still breaks inside itself, as before. An upstream candidate (Zed).

